			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add CancelOnDrop guard to provider forward calls\n\nReplace the direct `IPCProvider::SendRequestToSideCar` in `InvokeProvider`\nand `InvokeProviderMethod` with `ForwardCancellable`, a wrapper that runs\nthe Vine call on a detached `tokio::spawn` task guarded by a drop-triggered\nwatch signal. A new `CancelOnDrop` guard flips the signal when the calling\nfuture is dropped — from gRPC cancellation, typed-rail `CancelOperation`,\npeer disconnect, or any caller-side `select!` loss — so the detached task\ndelivers `CocoonService.CancelOperation` for the wire request id before\nexiting, terminating the side-car provider instead of computing a result\nnobody is waiting for.\n\nBoth provider-invocation paths now use `FnCancellable` from the Vine\nclient instead of the old blocking `SendRequestToSideCar`, eliminating\nthe `Arc<dyn IPCProvider>` / `Require()` dependency in both modules.",
			"SHA": "c1eb47dc38cbaf90ea0132444cba790bf24f046b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:20:51Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Mount CocoonService on shared port, invalidate extension install cache, pipe session ID to Cocoon\n\nMount `CocoonServiceServer` (typed `CocoonServiceImpl`) on the same tonic router as `MountainServiceServer` so both services share port 50051, replacing the previous unused-variable pattern. Derive `MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE` from `Vine::Client::Shared::MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE_BYTES` for lockstep configuration across the client-server boundary.\n\nCall `BumpScanGeneration()` on extension install and uninstall so that cached `extensions:getInstalled` responses from an earlier scan generation are invalidated, preventing stale builtins-only manifests from being served after user-path extensions are added or removed.\n\nInject `CocoonSessionId` into the Cocoon sidecar environment, carrying the same session UUID used for `telemetryInfo.sessionId` in initialization data. This lets `vscode.env.sessionId` resolve correctly in Cocoon before the extension-host handshake completes. Promote `SessionId()` from `fn` to `pub(crate) fn` for cross-module access.\n\nReplace the `dev_log`-based subscriber-lag warning in `VineSubscribeCommand` with a call to `Vine::Client::Shared::ReportNotificationLag`, upgrading a local log message to structured instrumentation that consumers can act upon.",
			"SHA": "7723552a9ff1ccd21397cddd7058838a788c775e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:06:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1855,
				11
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Background extension merge, ETag/304 scheme serving, gRPC cancellation, dialog action items\n\n**Extension scanner background merge** — Release the builtins-only manifest to `ScanReady` waiters immediately, then merge supplementary user-path extensions in a background `spawn_blocking` task. After merge, bump the `getInstalled` scan generation to invalidate any builtins-only cache entries, notify Cocoon of the delta via `$deltaExtensions`, emit `sky://extensions/installed` events for Sky's sidebar refresh, and re-run configuration merge so contributed `configuration` defaults from late-discovered extensions are applied. Full-scan path also bumps generation before notifying waiters.\n\n**Conditional GET (ETag/304) for scheme file handler** — Add `IfNoneMatchSatisfied` / `BuildNotModified` / `EmbeddedETag` / `CacheControlFor` helpers across all three serving paths (os-abs mmap, embedded asset resolver, fs-mmap StaticRoot). Fingerprinted bundle assets (`.js`, `.css`, `.woff2` under `Static/`) get `public, max-age=31536000, immutable`; everything else uses `public, max-age=3600` with ETag revalidation. The former separate `exists()`/`is_file()` stat() pair per request is eliminated — the mmap `LoadOrInsert` open is the existence probe, with `NotFound` falling through directly. Extract the sequential `replacen`-based path normalization into `NormalizePath` for a single-pass rewrite (query/fragment strip, `/out/` prefix removal, `Static/node_modules/` remap).\n\n**Background DNS server bind** — Move the Hickory DNS server start from a synchronous blocking call to `tauri::async_runtime::spawn_blocking`, overlapping the port probe with the rest of `AppLifecycleSetup`. `DnsPort` managed state is registered inside the background task rather than after the synchronous bind, eliminating a serialisation point during boot.\n\n**Optimized `.env.Land` candidate search** — Probe `.env.Land` up the exe ancestry first (most-likely path for non-TTY launches), removing redundant duplicate probes from the repo-layout section. Switch from separate `exists()` then `LoadEnvFile()` to using the `LoadEnvFile` open result as the existence check, eliminating one `stat()` per candidate.\n\n**Generation-based getInstalled cache invalidation** — Replace `OnceLock<Value>` per type with `Mutex<Option<(u64, Value)>>` keyed to a monotonic `SCAN_GENERATION` counter. The scanner bumps the generation after any post-`ScanReady` map mutation, so a builtins-only response cached during the early notify window is rebuilt from the merged extension map on the next call.\n\n**Per-request gRPC cancellation** — Register every `process_cocoon_request` call in `ActiveOperations` with a `CancellationToken`, race the dispatch future against it via `tokio::select!`. `cancel_operation` fires the token, the dispatch is dropped, and a `-32800` (request cancelled) error response is returned. The entry is unregistered on all exit paths, keeping the map bounded by in-flight requests. Validation and deserialization errors now carry structured `error.data` with the method name and detail.\n\n**Cocoon message dialog action buttons** — Add `repeated string Items` to the `ShowMessageRequest` protobuf message and propagate through `ShowErrorMessage`, `ShowInformationMessage`, and `ShowWarningMessage` so Cocoon's extension host can present action-button labels alongside native dialogs.\n\n**README badge fix** — Remove the ProtocolBuffers icon from the gRPC badge row, switching to a plain tonic badge.",
